  - id: that_which_defileth
    displayName: That Which Defileth
    flavorText: Jesus teaches the multitude that defilement comes not from unwashed
      hands but from the evil that proceeds out of a man's own heart.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: "Delivered first to the multitude and then explained privately to the
      disciples, this teaching relocates true defilement away from external ritual
      failure (eating with unwashed hands, the disputed tradition of the elders in
      7:1-13) to the internal condition of the heart \u2014 nothing entering a man
      from without can defile him, but the evil thoughts and deeds that proceed out
      of a man from within do. It functions as Jesus's positive teaching answer to
      the Pharisees' and scribes' preceding accusation."
    deliveredByManagerId: jesus_mark
    managerId: defilement_teaching_mark
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 1299.3380544866975
