  - id: the_fig_trees_sign
    displayName: The Fig Tree's Sign
    flavorText: On the Mount of Olives, Jesus foretells the temple's destruction
      and coming tribulation, likening the season to a fig tree putting forth leaves.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: "Delivered privately to four of the Twelve in response to a prediction
      that the temple would be utterly destroyed, this teaching prepares the disciples
      for coming upheaval, warns against being deceived by false christs, describes
      the coming persecution and \"abomination of desolation,\" and repeatedly presses
      the point that no one knows the day or hour \u2014 the point is readiness and
      watchfulness, not calculation."
    deliveredByManagerId: jesus_mark
    managerId: olivet_discourse_mark
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 8060.611083047648
